error[E0409]: `==` cannot be applied to `!int`
 --> mem:///main.lu:3:13
  |
3 |     if 1 == n { print("s") }
  |             ^ this is `!int`
  |
  = note: `==` works on values.
  = note: a `!T` is two values, never one, and no operator reads it ([type.row.operand]): `?`,
    `else` and `match` are the whole of how a row is handled. Handle it first — `n? == …`,
    `(n else 0) == …` — and operate on what it yields.
